          "text": "{\"checks\":[{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-selected-reference\",\"evidence-delivered-portrait\",\"evidence-native-views\",\"evidence-exported-views\"],\"name\":\"identity\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Subject reads as the requested plush toy panda with black eye patches and a small green shoulder dragon companion. The delivered portrait and native/exported multiviews consistently show the same panda/dragon pairing and proportions (large head, compact toy body) without added props/clothing/scenery.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-native-views\",\"evidence-delivered-portrait\"],\"name\":\"appearance\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Native render matches the intended plush look: soft, short groomed fur with clean black/ivory boundaries, expressive eyes with catchlights, and a distinct green dragon with visible sculpted details (spines/wings/tail) that is not covered in panda fur.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-exported-views\",\"evidence-motion-00\",\"evidence-isolated-exported-toy_dance\"],\"name\":\"appearance\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Exported representation does not match the requested \u201csoft, neatly groomed short fur\u201d look: it shows conspicuous sparse/spiky card-like tufts and patchy coverage over the panda (notably on head/body), producing a rough, stubbly silhouette and visible flecking rather than a continuous plush undercoat. These artifacts are prominent in exported multiview and during motion, making the exported avatar read lower-quality/less plush than native.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-native-views\",\"evidence-exported-views\"],\"name\":\"framing\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Full character (panda + perched dragon) is visible in front/side/back/three-quarter views for both native and exported. No extra props/clothing/text/pedestal/scenery are present.\"}],\"limitations\":[\"Motion evidence is a contact-sheet style sampling; it does not prove continuous-time collisions, ground contact, balance, or seamless looping across all frames (even if endpoints match).\",\"Only one isolated \u2018greatest_recorded_edge_stretch\u2019 pose is provided per representation; localized deformation/clipping elsewhere in the clip could be missed.\"],\"required_repairs\":[\"Fix exported fur/portable coat appearance to match the intended plush short-fur look: eliminate the obvious sparse spiky card tips and patchy coverage (especially on the panda head and torso). Target a denser, more even short pile with a cleaner silhouette and fewer visible individual card protrusions in exported views and during motion.\",\"Re-check exported motion appearance after fur fix to ensure the panda surface does not show conspicuous bald flecks/patches or harsh card artifacts during the dance frames.\"],\"state_reviews\":[{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\",\"evidence-isolated-native-toy_dance\",\"evidence-isolated-exported-toy_dance\",\"action-audit-toy_dance\"],\"id\":\"toy_dance\",\"meaning_passed\":false,\"motion_passed\":true,\"reason\":\"The clip shows real pose changes (sways/leans and some arm/head articulation). However, the requested \u201csmall whole-body hops\u201d are not clearly readable as hops from the provided motion contact sheet; the feet appear largely planted with no obvious up/down hop moments visible at the sampled frames. Additionally, exported fur artifacts are prominent during the motion, harming the intended plush presentation even when the motion itself changes.\",\"requirement_reviews\":[{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"three_beats_rhythm\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Across the sampled frames, the panda alternates side-to-side leaning/weight shifts multiple times over the 4 seconds, reading as repeated beats rather than a single sway.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"hops_and_sways\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Side-to-side sways are visible, but the \u2018small whole-body hops\u2019 are not clearly readable as hops in the provided sampled frames; the motion looks primarily like leaning/swaying with minimal apparent vertical lift.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"arm_swings\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Both arms change pose in coordination with the side-to-side beats (hands/forearms shift position across the sampled times), reading as toy-like arm swinging rather than remaining static.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"head_tilts\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Head/neck orientation changes are visible across the sampled frames (gentle tilts accompanying the sways).\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"dragon_attached\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"The green dragon remains perched on the shoulder throughout the sampled frames with no visible separation, flight, or drifting away; it follows the panda\u2019s body movement.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"return_body_pose\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"The final sampled frame visually matches the starting overall pose closely (body returns to the initial stance/orientation).\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"return_arm_pose\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Arms appear to return to their starting relaxed position by the end frame rather than holding a final gesture.\"},{\"evidence_ids\":[\"evidence-motion-00\"],\"id\":\"return_head_pose\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Head appears to return near-neutral at the end, matching the starting orientation closely.\"}]}],\"summary\":\"Native appearance meets the plush panda + perched green dragon brief, but exported fur/portable coat renders with conspicuous spiky/sparse card artifacts and patchiness that break the requested soft, neatly groomed short-fur look. The toy dance shows readable sways/tilts and returns to start, but the required \u2018small whole-body hops\u2019 are not clearly readable from the provided motion evidence. Requires repair before acceptance.\",\"verdict\":\"repair\"}"
        }
